63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID115","SecondaryAttribute":"What features were most important in comparing the fit to the data?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>What features were most important in comparing the fit to the data?<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q3b","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"What features were most important in comparing the fit to the data?","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID115"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID116","SecondaryAttribute":"What do you think Group 2 should do next?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"What do you think Group 2 should do next?","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q3c","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"What do you think Group 2 should do next?","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID116"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID117","SecondaryAttribute":"Which items below best reflect your reasoning?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which items below best reflect your reasoning?","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q3e","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Which items below best reflect your reasoning?","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID117","DataVisibility":{"Private":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID118","SecondaryAttribute":"You may use this space to explain or elaborate on any of your answers thus far. ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"You may use this space to explain or elaborate on any of your answers thus far.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q3f","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","InputWidth":680,"InputHeight":144},"QuestionDescription":"You may use this space to explain or elaborate on any of your answers thus far. ","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID118","DataVisibility":{"Private":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID119","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q3t","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","MinSeconds":"0","MaxSeconds":"0"},"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID119"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID120","SecondaryAttribute":"Summary \u00a0 Group 1:\u00a0 Method: 10 trials of 5 oscillations for 2 different masses and compared k\u00a0val","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Summary<\/strong><\/span><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Group 1:&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Method: 10 trials of 5 oscillations for 2 different masses and compared <em>k<\/em>&nbsp;values:<br \/>\nWith 30 g mass:&nbsp;<em>k<\/em> =&nbsp;4.0857 +\/- 0.08067 N\/m<\/div>\n\n<div>With 50 g mass:&nbsp;<em>k<\/em> =&nbsp;4.1872 +\/-&nbsp;0.06745 N\/m<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Group 2:<br \/>\nMethod:&nbsp;2&nbsp;trials of 5 oscillations for 10 different masses and compared the data to a model equation:&nbsp;<br \/>\nWith&nbsp;intercept set to 0:&nbsp;<em>k&nbsp;<\/em>= 4.0535 +\/-&nbsp;0.07005 N\/m<br \/>\nWith intercept not fixed at 0:&nbsp;<em>k <\/em>= 4.6274 +\/-&nbsp;0.1587 N\/m<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Click <a href=\"https:\/\/cornell.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_cVnx10pGM7eFWZL\">here<\/a> to see the intro again, <a href=\"https:\/\/stanforduniversity.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_6niQ1OxSRh2yzfn\">here<\/a> to see Group 1&#39;s lab book, <a href=\"https:\/\/cornell.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_cBxN0D7vM38e9SJ\">here<\/a> to see Group 2&#39;s initial lab book notes, and <a href=\"https:\/\/cornell.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_bdUNvDdSulgPuMR\">here<\/a> to see Group 2&#39;s second set of lab book notes.<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q4","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Summary \u00a0 Group 1:\u00a0 Method: 10 trials of 5 oscillations for 2 different masses and compared k\u00a0val...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID120"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID121","SecondaryAttribute":"Which group do you think did a better job of testing the model?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which group do you think did a better job of testing the model?","DataExportTag":"Q4a","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Which group do you think did a better job of testing the model?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Group 1"},"2":{"Display":"Group 2"},"3":{"Display":"Both the same"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID121"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID122","SecondaryAttribute":"What features are most important for evaluating the two groups?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>What features are most important for evaluating the two groups?<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q4b","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"What features are most important for evaluating the two groups?","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID122"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID123","SecondaryAttribute":"You may use this space to explain or elaborate on any of your answers thus far. ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"You may use this space to explain or elaborate on any of your answers thus far.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q4c","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","InputWidth":680,"InputHeight":147},"QuestionDescription":"You may use this space to explain or elaborate on any of your answers thus far. ","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID123"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID124","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q4t","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","MinSeconds":"0","MaxSeconds":"0"},"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID124"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID13","SecondaryAttribute":"Below are the notes Team Panda made in their lab book. You will then be asked about their data an...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<style type=\"text\/css\">table#t01 th {\n  text-align: center;\n background-color: black;\n color: white;\n}\ntable#t01 td {\n  text-align: right;\n}\ntable#t01 tr:nth-child(even) {\n background-color: #eee;\n}\ntable#t01 tr:nth-child(odd){\n background-color: #fff;\n}\n<\/style>\n<div>Below are the notes Team Panda made in their lab book. You will then be asked about their data and methods.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n<strong><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Team Panda: Lab book notes<\/span><\/span><br>\n<span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><u>Method<\/u><\/span><\/span><\/strong><br>\n<span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">To test the model (<i>T=2<\/i>\u213c\u221a(<i>m\u2044k<\/i>)), we found the period, <i>T<\/i>, for two different masses, then calculated and compared the two <i>k<\/i>-values (the values should be the same because it's the same spring). <\/span><\/span>\n\n<ul>\n <li><span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Put 20 g on the holder (holder is 10 g, so total is 30 g).<\/span><\/span><\/li>\n <li><span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Use the stopwatch to measure the time for 5 bounces (periods).<\/span><\/span><\/li>\n <li><span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Divide the time by 5 to get the period, <i> T<\/i>.<\/span><\/span><\/li>\n <li><span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Repeat 10 times, find the mean period and the&nbsp;uncertainty in the mean period. <\/span><\/span><\/li>\n <li><span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Repeat with 40 g on the holder (total of 50 g hanging). <\/span><\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<u><strong><span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"> Data<\/span><\/span> <\/strong><\/u><br>\n<span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The table shows our data for each mass. First column for each mass is the total time for five bounces. Second column is the period (total time divided by five).<\/span><\/span>\n\n<table id=\"t01\" style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th colspan=\"2\">Total mass = 30 g<\/th>\n   <th colspan=\"2\">Total mass = 50 g<\/th>\n  <\/tr>\n <\/thead>\n <tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td>Time for 5 bounces (s)<\/td>\n   <td>Period (s)<\/td>\n   <td>Time for 5 bounces (s)<\/td>\n   <td>Period (s)<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.78<\/td>\n   <td>0.556<\/td>\n   <td>3.39<\/td>\n   <td>0.678<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.68<\/td>\n   <td>0.536<\/td>\n   <td>3.35<\/td>\n   <td>0.670<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.76<\/td>\n   <td>0.552<\/td>\n   <td>3.40<\/td>\n   <td>0.680<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.70<\/td>\n   <td>0.540<\/td>\n   <td>3.42<\/td>\n   <td>0.684<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.67<\/td>\n   <td>0.534<\/td>\n   <td>3.40<\/td>\n   <td>0.680<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.82<\/td>\n   <td>0.564<\/td>\n   <td>3.45<\/td>\n   <td>0.690<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.66<\/td>\n   <td>0.532<\/td>\n   <td>3.31<\/td>\n   <td>0.662<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.72<\/td>\n   <td>0.544<\/td>\n   <td>3.55<\/td>\n   <td>0.710<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.56<\/td>\n   <td>0.512<\/td>\n   <td>3.60<\/td>\n   <td>0.720<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>2.57<\/td>\n   <td>0.514<\/td>\n   <td>3.46<\/td>\n   <td>0.692<\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n <\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<br>\n<span style=\"font-family:Courier New,Courier,monospace;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Average period for 30 g mass = <i>0.5384 \u00b1 0.00531 s <\/i><br>\n=&gt;&nbsp;<i>k<\/i>-value = <i>4\u213c<sup>2<\/sup>m\/T<sup>2<\/sup><\/i> = <i> 4.086 \u00b1 0.0807 N\/m <\/i><br>\nAverage period for 50 g mass = <i>0.6866 \u00b1 0.00553 s <\/i><br>\n=&gt;&nbsp;<i>k<\/i>-value = <i>4\u213c<sup>2<\/sup>m\/T<sup>2<\/sup><\/i> = <i> 4.187 \u00b1 0.0675 N\/m <\/i> <\/span><\/span>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Below are the notes Team Panda made in their lab book. You will then be asked about their data an...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID13","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID136","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Qt1","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","MinSeconds":"0","MaxSeconds":"0"},"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID136"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID14","SecondaryAttribute":"What do you think Team Panda should say about whether their data agree with the model?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"What do you think Team Panda should say about whether their data agree with the model?","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1a","QuestionID":"QID14","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"What do you think Team Panda should say about whether their data agree with the model?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"The data support the model."},"2":{"Display":"The data refute the model."},"3":{"Display":"There is not enough evidence to say either way."},"5":{"Display":"The data neither support nor refute the model."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","5","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID160","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","MinSeconds":"0","MaxSeconds":"0"},"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Timing","DataExportTag":"QtIDandName","QuestionID":"QID160","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":21,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID166","SecondaryAttribute":"What features were most important in comparing the fit to the data? Please select no more than 3...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>What features were most important in comparing the fit to the data?<\/p>Please select no more than 3 options.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q3b","QuestionID":"QID166","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"MACOL","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","NumColumns":2,"TextPosition":"inline"},"QuestionDescription":"What features were most important in comparing the fit to the data? Please select no more than 3...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"How well the data fall in a straight line","InputHeight":29,"InputWidth":147},"2":{"Display":"The way points are scattered above and below the line (random versus patterned)"},"6":{"Display":"The number of points with uncertainties (error bars) crossing the line"},"9":{"Display":"The number of outliers"},"10":{"Display":"Other (Please describe)","TextEntry":"true","InputWidth":138,"TextEntryForceResponse":true},"11":{"Display":"How close the points are to the line compared to the uncertainties"},"21":{"Display":"The number of points above the line compared to the number below the line"},"23":{"Display":"How close the points are to the line"},"29":{"Display":"The size of the uncertainty (or variability between data)"}},"ChoiceOrder":["11","21","2","23","9","29","6","1","10"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"QuestionID":"QID166","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID166\/SelectedChoicesCount","Operator":"LessThanOrEqual","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID166","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID166\/SelectedChoicesCount","RightOperand":"3","Type":"Expression","LogicType":"Question","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">What features were most important in comparing the fit to the data?Please select no more than 3 options.<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">q:\/\/QID166\/SelectedChoicesCount<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Less Than or Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 3 <\/span>"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"messageID":"MS_3EmA84tU2IfZVYx","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_1","libraryID":"UR_bOXilo3mscFKVRr","description":"Too many 3"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"PrivateData":false,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID172","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DataExportTag":"Q1d","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"MAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","NumColumns":2},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"The amount of data collected"},"3":{"Display":"The way they collected data (or the type or range of data collected)"},"4":{"Display":"The quality of the data"},"5":{"Display":"Other","TextEntry":"true","InputHeight":24,"InputWidth":203},"6":{"Display":"The way they presented their methods and data","InputHeight":24,"InputWidth":40}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","3","6","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"ChoiceRange","MinChoices":"","MaxChoices":"2"}},"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID172","DynamicChoicesData":[]}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID172040032","SecondaryAttribute":"Information about this survey You are invited to participate in a research project being conducte...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><b>Information about this survey<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">You are invited to participate in a research project being conducted by Prof. Natasha Holmes (Cornell University). The purpose of the research is to develop an assessment of students\u2019 critical thinking and reasoning about experimental physics data.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n<strong>What we will ask you to do:<\/strong> This survey poses a number of questions asking you to reason about experiments and data in physics.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Risks and discomforts:<\/strong> We do not anticipate any risks from participating in this research.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Benefits:<\/strong> There are no direct benefits other than the opportunity to learn, practice some new material, and contribute to future instructional innovations in physics lab courses.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Compensation for participation:<\/strong> You will either receive course credit or no compensation for your participation. If your instructor has assigned course credit for completing this survey, you must provide your name and student ID information at the end of the survey to receive this credit.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Privacy\/Confidentiality\/Data Security:<\/strong> Your identifying information will be kept with your survey data for the purposes of matching survey responses. Your instructor will have access to your responses at the end of semester\/quarter. Your identity will never be associated with your responses publicly.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Taking part is voluntary:<\/strong> You may choose whether to consent to having your survey data used for research purposes. Participation credit (if your instructor has assigned such credit) does not depend on any specific answers you provide in the survey or on whether you consent to have your answers used in research. You may complete this survey for your instructor without consenting to participate in the research. You must complete this survey for your instructor to obtain participation credit in your course (if applicable).<br>\n<br>\n<strong>If you have questions:<\/strong> If you have any questions about this study, please contact Prof. Natasha Holmes (ngh35@cornell.edu).&nbsp;If you have any questions or concerns regarding your rights as a subject in this study, you may contact the Institutional Review Board (IRB) for Human Participants at 607-255-6182 or access their website at http:\/\/www.irb.cornell.edu. You may also report your concerns or complaints anonymously through Ethicspoint online at www.hotline.cornell.edu or by calling toll free at 1-866-293-3077. Ethicspoint is an independent organization that serves as a liaison between the University and the person bringing the complaint so that anonymity can be ensured.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Reminder:<\/strong> If your instructor has assigned course credit for completing this survey, you must provide your name and student ID information at the end of the survey to receive this credit, independent of consenting to participate in the research study.<\/p>","DataExportTag":"IRBInfo","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Information about this survey You are invited to participate in a research project being conducte...","GradingData":[],"Language":[],"ChoiceOrder":[],"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p style=\"text-align: center; \">\n\t<span style=\"font-size:19px;\">Informed Consent Form<\/span><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Introduction<br>\n\t<br>\n\t<\/strong><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tThis study attempts to collect information about differences in individual perception of older role models\u2026<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Procedures<\/strong><br><\/p>\n<p>\n\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tYou will be shown a photograph and short biography of a simulated potential professor and asked to complete a short questionnaire about the person in the photograph. The questionnaire consists of 15 questions and will take approximately 20 minutes or less. Questions are designed to determine how you expect a simulated professor would behave in a class setting based on your past experience. This questionnaire will be conducted with an online Qualtrics-created survey.<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Risks\/Discomforts<\/strong><br>&nbsp; &nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tRisks are minimal for involvement in this study. However, you may feel emotionally uneasy when asked to make judgments based on the photograph and biography provided. Although we do not expect any harm to come upon any participants due to electronic malfunction of the computer, it is possible though extremely rare and uncommon.<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Benefits<\/strong><br>&nbsp; &nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tThere are no direct benefits for participants. However, it is hoped that through your participation, researchers will learn more about which qualities students prefer in professors.<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Confidentiality<\/strong><br>&nbsp; &nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tAll data obtained from participants will be kept confidential and will only be reported in an aggregate format (by reporting only combined results and never reporting individual ones). All questionnaires will be concealed, and no one other than then primary investigator and assistant researches listed below will have access to them. The data collected will be stored in the HIPPA-compliant, Qualtrics-secure database until it has been deleted by the primary investigator.<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Compensation<\/strong><br>&nbsp; &nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tThere is no direct compensation, however, participants may earn extra academic credit, at the discretion of their professors.<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Participation<\/strong><br><\/p>\n<p>\n\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tParticipation in this research study is completely voluntary. You have the right to withdraw at anytime or refuse to participate entirely without jeopardy to your academic status, GPA or standing with the university. If you desire to withdraw, please close your internet browser and notify the principal investigator at this email: (email). &nbsp;Or, if you prefer, inform the principal investigator as you leave. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Questions about the Research<\/strong><br>&nbsp; &nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tIf you have questions regarding this study, you may contact (principal investigator), at 555-555-5555, principleinvestigator@fakeemail555.com or (assistant 1) 666-666-6666, assistant1@fakeemail555.com, (assistant 2) 777-777-7777, assistant2@fakeemail555.com.<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p>&nbsp;<\/o:p><o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\t<strong>Questions about your Rights as Research Participants<\/strong><br><\/p>\n<p>\n\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<p>\n\tIf you have questions you do not feel comfortable asking the researcher, you may contact (Dr Mentoring Professor), 222-222-2222, 1030 SWKT, drmentoringprofessor@greatuniversity.edu. Or contact the director of (your University)'s Institutional Review Board, Bob Irb, 888-888-8888, bobirb@greatuniversity.edu.&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>\n\t<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>\n<div style=\"text-align: right;\">\n\t<input onclick=\"window.print()\" type=\"button\" value=\"Print\"><\/div>","QuestionID":"QID172040032","DefaultChoices":false,"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID172040033","SecondaryAttribute":"Statement of Consent:\u00a0I have read and understood the above information. I consent to take part in..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Statement of Consent:&nbsp;<\/strong>I have read and understood the above information. I consent to take part in the study.<\/span><\/p>","DataExportTag":"QConsent","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Statement of Consent:\u00a0I have read and understood the above information. I consent to take part in...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Yes"},"2":{"Display":"No"}},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"ChoiceOrder":["1","2"],"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<P>\n I have read, understood, and printed a copy of, the above consent form and desire of my own free will to participate in this study.&nbsp;<\/P>","QuestionID":"QID172040033","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1,"RecodeValues":{"1":"1","2":"0"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_3ej1HpRwjR63YKa","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID18","SecondaryAttribute":"Which items below more specifically reflect your reasoning in Q1c? Please select no more than 3 o...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which items below more specifically reflect your reasoning in Q1c? Please select no more than 3 options.&nbsp;<br><div>Note: There are multiple options for the same idea that allow you to indicate whether it was good or bad.<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1da","QuestionID":"QID18","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"MACOL","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","NumColumns":3,"TextPosition":"inline"},"QuestionDescription":"Which items below more specifically reflect your reasoning in Q1c? Please select no more than 3 o...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"They took too few repeated trials for each mass","DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"Question","QuestionID":"QID172","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID172\/SelectableChoice\/1","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID172","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID172\/SelectableChoice\/1","Typ